# Level-5 Tutorial: From Admitted Source to Replay

## Prerequisites

Identify the exact consumer subject, toolchain, canonical semantic source, and bounded execution environment.

## Admitted inputs

Record the ontology/configuration inputs that constitute the consumer's admitted `O*`. Raw input is not execution authority.

## Executable path

Follow the real path used by the consumer:

```text
parse -> admit/refuse -> construct -> verify -> receipt -> replay
```

Document the exact commands that exercise this path. The consuming project must execute them in its own qualification court; Markdown command presence is not execution evidence.

## Verification

State the exact-subject verifier and expected success condition. Generated existence alone is insufficient.

## Receipt and replay

Record how the consequence is bound to subject identity, authority, consequence, and replay. Verify the receipt and replay the same admitted subject.

## Falsifiers

Include at least one domain-specific negative witness that must be refused or cause standing to fall.

## Rollback

Explain the reversible path back to the previous admitted subject without widening authority.

## Standing

This tutorial is a generated documentation surface. Its commands acquire ALIVE standing only when observed against the exact admitted consumer subject.
